      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know that other test here have comments, but I often don\u0027t see the value of it.\nHere we are repeating the name of the test, and no need to repeat test on the test name neither :/\n\nA few months ago I found out about go/unit-testing-practices#naming and I really like the idea of it, for this test that could be: (dropping an idea, feel free to adapt_\n\n`startBleOnly_whenScanManagerRefactorFlagIsOn_onlyStartScanController()`\n\nWhen you only have one test it looks weird, but when you start to have a couple it\u0027s add values.\nOne of recent example of this kind of test writing can be found in the [satellite listener](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/service/src/satellite/ModeListenerTest.kt)\n\nDon\u0027t make any change if you don\u0027t want to, as this is very personal preference and there is no wide adoption in the team (yet ;) )",
